It should not matter.

> - Do I have to issue some "connect" or "dial in" command to get minicom
> connecting to the Alhpa?

You are not dialing or "connecting" anywhere.  You may want to turn off
DTR handling in you terminal emulator.  Your connection is permanent.

OTOH if you are seeing '>>>' prompt, instead of a blue screen, and you
can type something on a console and results are echoed to your screen
then you are NOT on a serial console.  At least with some versions of
SRM if you are on a serial console then hitting Return key one or more
times on a local keyboard is switching to a "graphics" console (at least
for the current session and then you can use 'set console' to do that
more permanent).

Try typing at '>>>' prompt things like 'help more' and 'help show*|
more' Various show commands should tell you what is recognized, or not,
on your system.  Are all your disks and CDs SCSI?  What controller?  It
may be a type not recognized by your firmware.  Is this the latest
available version for your board?  Does 'set os_type nt' allows you to
switch to ARC console?  You may need to reboot for that and depending on
ROMs you may have space for only one firmware set.  Other than that some
cables (controller connection, power) may be not plugged properly. Last
but not least you still have an access to a floppy so if nothing works
you can always reload that other console for your board.

> matthias (who still hopes to see his Alpha resurrected!)

It does not seem to be dead, by a long mile, from your description.

